      "message": "out of curiosity, why not encode directly into a YAML syntax tree? given that the decoder goes straight from YAML syntax to cue/ast, I would hope that the encoder can also go from cue/ast (or cue.Value) straight to YAML syntax, be it a node tree or a token stream.\n\nadding an extra step in the form of a \"Go value tree\" is perhaps nice in terms of isolation, but I worry a bit that it adds a whole bunch of allocations.",
